  "notes": "Herdr fork preview (wwelder/herdr): gram is the owner's inbox\n\nSource: d1931bb06b04abde228518ebe7fd217ae0dd6c4d.\n\n- Gram now collects what needs the owner, with `kind`, `pane_id`, `session` and `resolved` on each entry:\n  - `blocked`: an agent's question. It is resolved in place once the agent moves on, its pane exits, or the pane is closed.\n  - `recap`: the agent's final reply at the end of each turn.\n  - `died`: the agent's pane died.\n  These entries are owner-only and never push on their own. At the store cap they are evicted before real messages.\n- `codex exec` runs are subagents. `agent.list` and `agent.get` mark them with `subagent: true`. They are hidden from the agent panel, pushes, toasts and Live Activity, and they get no gram entries.\n- A `--critical` gram now reaches devices that have gram alerts off.\n\nAll five assets were built by the manual Build artifacts workflow (run 41928856071).\n\nUpdate with `herdr update` on the preview channel.",
